---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About | MathMyRate" description="What MathMyRate is, what it is not, and how it operates.">
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-5xl font-bold leading-none md:text-6xl">A calculator, not an oracle.</h1>
    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
      <p>MathMyRate is a free suite of pricing calculators for freelancers and digital-product sellers. It exists to answer two practical questions, what to charge and what you keep, with the assumptions attached, so you can disagree with the inputs instead of the tool.</p>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">What this is</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Client-side calculators that run in your browser. Fee rules are limited to documented, officially sourced scenarios, and each page links to its source with a review date. There are no accounts, no paywalls, and no ads.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">What this is not</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">It is not a tax, accounting, or legal service, and it is not affiliated with or endorsed by Stripe, PayPal, Gumroad, or Lemon Squeezy. Results are estimates that depend entirely on the inputs you provide. For decisions that matter, talk to a qualified professional who knows your situation.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">How it is built</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">The calculation engine is a framework-independent package using exact integer arithmetic. This site is a static build; public calculations happen in your browser and are not sent to a server.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
